3幕 第4场","n":1584},{"h":"Act 4, Scene 1","zh":"第4幕 第1场","n":2190},{"h":"Act 4, Scene 2","zh":"第4幕 第2场","n":2013},{"h":"Act 4, Scene 3","zh":"第4幕 第3场","n":877},{"h":"Act 5, Scene 1","zh":"第5幕 第1场","n":1062},{"h":"Act 5, Scene 2","zh":"第5幕 第2场","n":3021}]},{"a":"shakespeare","id":"sonnets","t":"Sonnets","z":"十四行诗","k":"Poems","zk":"诗","s":"154 首十四行诗，每首 14 行。最有名的是第 18 首「Shall I compare thee to a summer’s day?」。","src":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/william-shakespeare/poetry","n":17589,"parts":[{"h":"Sonnet 1","zh":"第1首","n":106,"first":"From fairest creatures we desire increase,"},{"h":"Sonnet 2","zh":"第2首","n":116,"first":"When forty winters shall besiege thy brow,"},{"h":"Sonnet 3","zh":"第3首","n":116,"first":"Look in thy glass, and tell the face thou viewest"},{"h":"Sonnet 4","zh":"第4首","n":101,"first":"Unthrifty loveliness, why dost thou spend"},{"h":"Sonnet 5","zh":"第5首","n":105,"first":"Those hours, that with gentle work did frame"},{"h":"Sonnet 6","zh":"第6首","n":110,"first":"Then let not winter’s ragged hand deface"},{"h":"Sonnet 7","zh":"第7首","n":103,"first":"Lo! in the orient when the gracious light"},{"h":"Sonnet 8","zh":"第8首","n":111,"first":"Music to hear, why hear’st thou music sadly?"},{"h":"Sonnet 9","zh":"第9首","n":117,"first":"Is it for fear to wet a widow’s eye"},{"h":"Sonnet 10","zh":"第10首","n":113,"first":"For shame! deny that thou bear’st love to any,"},{"h":"Sonnet 11","zh":"第11首","n":116,"first":"As fast as thou shalt wane, so fast thou growest"},{"h":"Sonnet 12","zh":"第12首","n":118,"first":"When I do count the clock that tells the time,"},{"h":"Sonnet 13","zh":"第13首","n":108,"first":"O, that you were yourself! but, love, you are"},{"h":"Sonnet 14","zh":"第14首","n":112,"first":"Not from the stars do I my judgement pluck;"},{"h":"Sonnet 15","zh":"第15首","n":111,"first":"When I consider everything that grows"},{"h":"Sonnet 16","zh":"第16首","n":108,"first":"But wherefore do not you a mightier way"},{"h":"Sonnet 17","zh":"第17首","n":124,"first":"Who will believe my verse in time to come,"},{"h":"Sonnet 18","zh":"第18首","n":114,"first":"Shall I compare thee to a summer’s day?"},{"h":"Sonnet 19","zh":"第19首","n":117,"first":"Devouring Time, blunt thou the lion’s paws,"},{"h":"Sonnet 20","zh":"第20首","n":115,"first":"A woman’s face with Nature’s own hand painted"},{"h":"Sonnet 21","zh":"第21首","n":118,"first":"So is it not with me as with that Muse"},{"h":"Sonnet 22","zh":"第22首","n":122,"first":"My glass shall not persuade me I am old,"},{"h":"Sonnet 23","zh":"第23首","n":114,"first":"As an unperfect actor on the stage"},{"h":"Sonnet 24","zh":"第24首","n":121,"first":"Mine eye hath play’d the painter and hath stell’d"},{"h":"Sonnet 25","zh":"第25首","n":108,"first":"Let those who are in favour with their stars"},{"h":"Sonnet 26","zh":"第26首","n":118,"first":"Lord of my love, to whom in vassalage"},{"h":"Sonnet 27","zh":"第27首","n":111,"first":"Weary with toil, I haste me to my bed,"},{"h":"Sonnet 28","zh":"第28首","n":117,"first":"How can I then return in happy plight,"},{"h":"Sonnet 29","zh":"第29首","n":114,"first":"When, in disgrace with fortune and men’s eyes,"},{"h":"Sonnet 30","zh":"第30首","n":117,"first":"When to the sessions of sweet silent thought"},{"h":"Sonnet 31","zh":"第31首","n":115,"first":"Thy bosom is endeared with all hearts,"},{"h":"Sonnet 32","zh":"第32首","n":116,"first":"If thou survive my well-contented day,"},{"h":"Sonnet 33","zh":"第33首","n":110,"first":"Full many a glorious morning have I seen"},{"h":"Sonnet 34","zh":"第34首","n":121,"first":"Why didst thou promise such a beauteous day"},{"h":"Sonnet 35","zh":"第35首","n":106,"first":"No more be grieved at that which thou hast done:"},{"h":"Sonnet 36","zh":"第36首","n":113,"first":"Let me confess that we two must be twain,"},{"h":"Sonnet 37","zh":"第37首","n":116,"first":"As a decrepit father takes delight"},{"h":"Sonnet 38","zh":"第38首","n":112,"first":"How can my Muse want subject to invent,"},{"h":"Sonnet 39","zh":"第39首","n":119,"first":"O, how thy worth with manners may I sing,"},{"h":"Sonnet 40","zh":"第40首","n":120,"first":"Take all my loves, my love, yea, take them all;"},{"h":"Sonnet 41","zh":"第41首","n":110,"first":"Those pretty wrongs that liberty commits,"},{"h":"Sonnet 42","zh":"第42首","n":130,"first":"That thou hast her, it is not all my grief,"},{"h":"Sonnet 43","zh":"第43首","n":122,"first":"When most I wink, then do mine eyes best see,"},{"h":"Sonnet 44","zh":"第44首","n":117,"first":"If the dull substance of my flesh were thought,"},{"h":"Sonnet 45","zh":"第45首","n":106,"first":"The other two, slight air and purging fire,"},{"h":"Sonnet 46","zh":"第46首","n":115,"first":"Mine eye and heart are at a mortal war"},{"h":"Sonnet 47","zh":"第47首","n":122,"first":"Betwixt mine eye and heart a league is took,"},{"h":"Sonnet 48","zh":"第48首","n":117,"first":"How careful was I, when I took my way,"},{"h":"Sonnet 49","zh":"第49首","n":113,"first":"Against that time, if ever that time come,"},{"h":"Sonnet 50","zh":"第50首","n":118,"first":"How heavy do I journey on the way,"},{"h":"Sonnet 51","zh":"第51首","n":120,"first":"Thus can my love excuse the slow offence"},{"h":"Sonnet 52","zh":"第52首","n":111,"first":"So am I as the rich, whose blessed key"},{"h":"Sonnet 53","zh":"第53首","n":105,"first":"What is your substance, whereof are you made,"},{"h":"Sonnet 54","zh":"第54首","n":112,"first":"O, how much more doth beauty beauteous seem"},{"h":"Sonnet 55","zh":"第55首","n":107,"first":"Not marble, nor the gilded monuments"},{"h":"Sonnet 56","zh":"第56首","n":116,"first":"Sweet love, renew thy force; be it not said"},{"h":"Sonnet 57","zh":"第57首","n":119,"first":"Being your slave, what should I do but tend"},{"h":"Sonnet 58","zh":"第58首","n":113,"first":"That god forbid that made me first your slave,"},{"h":"Sonnet 59","zh":"第59首","n":109,"first":"If there be nothing new, but that which is"},{"h":"Sonnet 60","zh":"第60首","n":108,"first":"Like as the waves make towards the pebbled shore,"},{"h":"Sonnet 61","zh":"第61首","n":121,"first":"Is it thy will thy image should keep open"},{"h":"Sonnet 62","zh":"第62首","n":110,"first":"Sin of self-love possesseth all mine eye"},{"h":"Sonnet 63","zh":"第63首","n":110,"first":"Against my love shall be, as I am now,"},{"h":"Sonnet 64","zh":"第64首","n":112,"first":"When I have seen by Time’s fell hand defaced"},{"h":"Sonnet 65","zh":"第65首","n":113,"first":"Since brass, nor stone, nor earth, nor boundless sea,"},{"h":"Sonnet 66","zh":"第66首","n":91,"first":"Tired with all these, for restful death I cry,"},{"h":"Sonnet 67","zh":"第67首","n":106,"first":"Ah! wherefore with infection should he live,"},{"h":"Sonnet 68","zh":"第68首","n":108,"first":"Thus is his cheek the map of days outworn,"},{"h":"Sonnet 69","zh":"第69首","n":123,"first":"Those parts of thee that the world’s eye doth view"},{"h":"Sonnet 70","zh":"第70首","n":110,"first":"That thou art blamed shall not be thy defect,"},{"h":"Sonnet 71","zh":"第71首","n":123,"first":"No longer mourn for me when I am dead"},{"h":"Sonnet 72","zh":"第72首","n":119,"first":"O, lest the world should task you to recite"},{"h":"Sonnet 73","zh":"第73首","n":122,"first":"That time of year thou mayst in me behold"},{"h":"Sonnet 74","zh":"第74首","n":113,"first":"But be contented: when that fell arrest"},{"h":"Sonnet 75","zh":"第75首","n":118,"first":"So are you to my thoughts as food to life,"},{"h":"Sonnet 76","zh":"第76首","n":115,"first":"Why is my verse so barren of new pride,"},{"h":"Sonnet 77","zh":"第77首","n":107,"first":"Thy glass will show thee how thy beauties wear,"},{"h":"Sonnet 78","zh":"第78首","n":110,"first":"So oft have I invoked thee for my Muse"},{"h":"Sonnet 79","zh":"第79首","n":116,"first":"Whilst I alone did call upon thy aid,"},{"h":"Sonnet 80","zh":"第80首","n":117,"first":"O, how I faint when I of you do write,"},{"h":"Sonnet 81","zh":"第81首","n":118,"first":"Or I shall live your epitaph to make,"},{"h":"Sonnet 82","zh":"第82首","n":107,"first":"I grant thou wert not married to my Muse"},{"h":"Sonnet 83","zh":"第83首","n":116,"first":"I never saw that you did painting need"},{"h":"Sonnet 84","zh":"第84首","n":115,"first":"Who is it that says most? which can say more"},{"h":"Sonnet 85","zh":"第85首","n":112,"first":"My tongue-tied Muse in manners holds her still,"},{"h":"Sonnet 86","zh":"第86首","n":110,"first":"Was it the proud full sail of his great verse,"},{"h":"Sonnet 87","zh":"第87首","n":117,"first":"Farewell! thou art too dear for my possessing,"},{"h":"Sonnet 88","zh":"第88首","n":113,"first":"When thou shalt be disposed to set me light"},{"h":"Sonnet 89","zh":"第89首","n":111,"first":"Say that thou didst forsake me for some fault,"},{"h":"Sonnet 90","zh":"第90首","n":122,"first":"Then hate me when thou wilt; if ever, now;"},{"h":"Sonnet 91","zh":"第91首","n":115,"first":"Some glory in their birth, some in their skill,"},{"h":"Sonnet 92","zh":"第92首","n":121,"first":"But do thy worst to steal thyself away,"},{"h":"Sonnet 93","zh":"第93首","n":114,"first":"So shall I live, supposing thou art true,"},{"h":"Sonnet 94","zh":"第94首","n":106,"first":"They that have power to hurt and will do none,"},{"h":"Sonnet 95","zh":"第95首","n":113,"first":"How sweet and lovely dost thou make the shame"},{"h":"Sonnet 96","zh":"第96首","n":120,"first":"Some say thy fault is youth, some wantonness;"},{"h":"Sonnet 97","zh":"第97首","n":107,"first":"How like a winter hath my absence been"},{"h":"Sonnet 98","zh":"第98首","n":118,"first":"From you have I been absent in the spring,"},{"h":"Sonnet 99","zh":"第99首","n":125,"first":"The forward violet thus did I chide:"},{"h":"Sonnet 100","zh":"第100首","n":110,"first":"Where art thou, Muse, that thou forget’st so long"},{"h":"Sonnet 101","zh":"第101首","n":114,"first":"O truant Muse, what shall be thy amends"},{"h":"Sonnet 102","zh":"第102首","n":117,"first":"My love is strengthen’d, though more weak in seeming;"},{"h":"Sonnet 103","zh":"第103首","n":118,"first":"Alack, what poverty my Muse brings forth,"},{"h":"Sonnet 104","zh":"第104首","n":118,"first":"To me, fair friend, you never can be old,"},{"h":"Sonnet 105","zh":"第105首","n":107,"first":"Let not my love be call’d idolatry,"},{"h":"Sonnet 106","zh":"第106首","n":110,"first":"When in the chronicle of wasted time"},{"h":"Sonnet 107","zh":"第107首","n":113,"first":"Not mine own fears, nor the prophetic soul"},{"h":"Sonnet 108","zh":"第108首","n":115,"first":"What’s in the brain that ink may character"},{"h":"Sonnet 109","zh":"第109首","n":115,"first":"O, never say that I was false of heart,"},{"h":"Sonnet 110","zh":"第110首","n":118,"first":"Alas, ’tis true I have gone here and there"},{"h":"Sonnet 111","zh":"第111首","n":110,"first":"O, for my sake do you with Fortune chide,"},{"h":"Sonnet 112","zh":"第112首","n":117,"first":"Your love and pity doth the impression fill"},{"h":"Sonnet 113","zh":"第113首","n":117,"first":"Since I left you, mine eye is in my mind;"},{"h":"Sonnet 114","zh":"第114首","n":114,"first":"Or whether doth my mind, being crown’d with you,"},{"h":"Sonnet 115","zh":"第115首","n":115,"first":"Those lines that I before have writ do lie,"},{"h":"Sonnet 116","zh":"第116首","n":110,"first":"Let me not to the marriage of true minds"},{"h":"Sonnet 117","zh":"第117首","n":111,"first":"Accuse me thus: that I have scanted all"},{"h":"Sonnet 118","zh":"第118首","n":113,"first":"Like as, to make our appetite more keen,"},{"h":"Sonnet 119","zh":"第119首","n":113,"first":"What potions have I drunk of Siren tears,"},{"h":"Sonnet 120","zh":"第120首","n":117,"first":"That you were once unkind befriends me now,"},{"h":"Sonnet 121","zh":"第121首","n":115,"first":"’Tis better to be vile than vile esteem’d,"},{"h":"Sonnet 122","zh":"第122首","n":105,"first":"Thy gift, thy tables, are within my brain"},{"h":"Sonnet 123","zh":"第123首","n":116,"first":"No, Time, thou shalt not boast that I do change:"},{"h":"Sonnet 124","zh":"第124首","n":110,"first":"If my dear love were but the child of state,"},{"h":"Sonnet 125","zh":"第125首","n":105,"first":"Were’t aught to me I bore the canopy,"},{"h":"Sonnet 126","zh":"第126首","n":96,"first":"O thou, my lovely boy, who in thy power"},{"h":"Sonnet 127","zh":"第127首","n":111,"first":"In the old age black was not counted fair,"},{"h":"Sonnet 128","zh":"第128首","n":111,"first":"How oft, when thou, my music, music play’st,"},{"h":"Sonnet 129","zh":"第129首","n":110,"first":"The expense of spirit in a waste of shame"},{"h":"Sonnet 130","zh":"第130首","n":123,"first":"My mistress’ eyes are nothing like the sun;"},{"h":"Sonnet 131","zh":"第131首","n":119,"first":"Thou art as tyrannous, so as thou art,"},{"h":"Sonnet 132","zh":"第132首","n":114,"first":"Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,"},{"h":"Sonnet 133","zh":"第133首","n":122,"first":"Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan"},{"h":"Sonnet 134","zh":"第134首","n":121,"first":"So, now I have confess’d that he is thine,"},{"h":"Sonnet 135","zh":"第135首","n":116,"first":"Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy “Will,”"},{"h":"Sonnet 136","zh":"第136首","n":125,"first":"If thy soul check thee that I come so near,"},{"h":"Sonnet 137","zh":"第137首","n":125,"first":"Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes,"},{"h":"Sonnet 138","zh":"第138首","n":118,"first":"When my love swears that she is made of truth"},{"h":"Sonnet 139","zh":"第139首","n":121,"first":"O, call not me to justify the wrong"},{"h":"Sonnet 140","zh":"第140首","n":121,"first":"Be wise as thou art cruel; do not press"},{"h":"Sonnet 141","zh":"第141首","n":118,"first":"In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,"},{"h":"Sonnet 142","zh":"第142首","n":118,"first":"Love is my sin and thy dear virtue hate,"},{"h":"Sonnet 143","zh":"第143首","n":119,"first":"Lo! as a careful housewife runs to catch"},{"h":"Sonnet 144","zh":"第144首","n":113,"first":"Two loves I have of comfort and despair,"},{"h":"Sonnet 145","zh":"第145首","n":97,"first":"Those lips that Love’s own hand did make"},{"h":"Sonnet 146","zh":"第146首","n":113,"first":"Poor soul, the centre of my sinful earth,"},{"h":"Sonnet 147","zh":"第147首","n":108,"first":"My love is as a fever, longing still"},{"h":"Sonnet 148","zh":"第148首","n":124,"first":"O me, what eyes hath Love put in my head,"},{"h":"Sonnet 149","zh":"第149首","n":117,"first":"Canst thou, O cruel! say I love thee not,"},{"h":"Sonnet 150","zh":"第150首","n":118,"first":"O, from what power hast thou this powerful might"},{"h":"Sonnet 151","zh":"第151首","n":119,"first":"Love is too young to know what conscience is;"},{"h":"Sonnet 152","zh":"第152首","n":125,"first":"In loving thee thou know’st I am forsworn,"},{"h":"Sonnet 153","zh":"第153首","n":112,"first":"Cupid laid by his brand, and fell asleep:"},{"h":"Sonnet 154","zh":"第154首","n":109,"first":"The little Love-god lying once asleep"}]},{"a":"aeschylus","id":"agamemnon","t":"Agamemnon","z":"阿伽门农","k":"Tragedy · Oresteia 1","zk":"悲剧 ·《俄瑞斯忒亚》之一","s":"特洛伊战争结束，阿伽门农凯旋回家。等着他的，是因为女儿被献祭而记恨了十年的妻子克吕泰涅斯特拉。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.01.0004","n":14356,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2032},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1796},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2495},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2128},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1255},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":2533},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":1093},{"h":"Part 8","zh":"第8部分","n":1024}]},{"a":"aeschylus","id":"libation-bearers","t":"The Libation Bearers","z":"奠酒人","k":"Tragedy · Oresteia 2","zk":"悲剧 ·《俄瑞斯忒亚》之二","s":"多年后，阿伽门农的儿子俄瑞斯忒斯回到故乡，在父亲墓前与姐姐厄勒克特拉重逢，两人决定为父报仇。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":9670,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2810},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2330},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1764},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1400},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1366}]},{"a":"aeschylus","id":"eumenides","t":"The Eumenides","z":"报仇神","k":"Tragedy · Oresteia 3","zk":"悲剧 ·《俄瑞斯忒亚》之三","s":"杀了母亲的俄瑞斯忒斯被复仇女神追赶，逃到雅典。雅典娜设立法庭审判此案——据说这是西方第一场陪审团审判。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":8893,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1367},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1344},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1592},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2583},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1140},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":867}]},{"a":"aeschylus","id":"prometheus-bound","t":"Prometheus Bound","z":"被缚的普罗米修斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"普罗米修斯为人类盗来天火，被宙斯锁在高加索的悬崖上。他知道一个关于宙斯命运的秘密，却宁死不说。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":9676,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1161},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2359},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1030},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":3279},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1847}]},{"a":"aeschylus","id":"persians","t":"The Persians","z":"波斯人","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"现存最早的希腊悲剧，写的是真实历史：波斯宫廷里，人们等来了大军在萨拉米斯海战惨败的消息。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":9009,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2249},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2680},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1059},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1677},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1344}]},{"a":"aeschylus","id":"seven-against-thebes","t":"Seven Against Thebes","z":"七将攻忒拜","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"俄狄浦斯的两个儿子争夺王位，被赶走的波吕尼刻斯带着七位将领攻打忒拜的七座城门。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":9055,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1002},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1426},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":984},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2559},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1083},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":991},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":1010}]},{"a":"aeschylus","id":"suppliant-maidens","t":"The Suppliant Maidens","z":"乞援人","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"达那俄斯的五十个女儿为了逃避逼婚，逃到阿尔戈斯向国王求助。国王必须在收留她们和避免战争之间做选择。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":8543,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2758},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1575},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1549},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2269},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":392}]},{"a":"sophocles","id":"oedipus-rex","t":"Oedipus the King","z":"俄狄浦斯王","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"忒拜城瘟疫流行，国王俄狄浦斯发誓要找出杀害前国王的凶手。他一步步追查，真相却指向了他自己。","src":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/sophocles/oedipus-rex/francis-storr","n":12193,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1257},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2549},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":3167},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1737},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":775},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":2708}]},{"a":"sophocles","id":"oedipus-at-colonus","t":"Oedipus at Colonus","z":"俄狄浦斯在科罗诺斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"失明流浪的老俄狄浦斯由女儿安提戈涅搀扶，来到雅典附近的科罗诺斯，在那里迎来生命的终点。","src":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/sophocles/oedipus-at-colonus/francis-storr","n":13136,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2539},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2483},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2948},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1252},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2476},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1438}]},{"a":"sophocles","id":"antigone","t":"Antigone","z":"安提戈涅","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"国王克瑞翁下令不许埋葬叛徒波吕尼刻斯。他的妹妹安提戈涅认为神的律法高于国王的命令，坚持埋葬了哥哥。","src":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/sophocles/antigone/francis-storr","n":9874,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":785},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1706},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1906},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1474},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1087},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1299},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":1617}]},{"a":"sophocles","id":"ajax","t":"Ajax","z":"埃阿斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"阿喀琉斯死后，他的铠甲判给了奥德修斯而不是埃阿斯。埃阿斯怒火中烧，被雅典娜蒙蔽了心智……","src":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/sophocles/ajax/francis-storr","n":11100,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1148},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1748},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1741},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2287},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2287},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1889}]},{"a":"sophocles","id":"electra-sophocles","t":"Electra","z":"厄勒克特拉","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"厄勒克特拉在宫中忍辱多年，等待弟弟俄瑞斯忒斯回来为父报仇。却有人带来了弟弟的死讯。","src":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/sophocles/electra/francis-storr","n":11315,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2145},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1339},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2184},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2180},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2454},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1013}]},{"a":"sophocles","id":"philoctetes","t":"Philoctetes","z":"菲罗克忒忒斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"被希腊人丢在荒岛上十年的菲罗克忒忒斯，手里有赫拉克勒斯的神弓。奥德修斯带着年轻的涅俄普托勒摩斯来骗取这把弓。","src":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/sophocles/philoctetes/francis-storr","n":11517,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":3039},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2307},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":3130},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":3041}]},{"a":"sophocles","id":"trachiniae","t":"The Trachiniae","z":"特拉基斯妇女","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"赫拉克勒斯的妻子得知丈夫爱上了别人，送去一件涂了「爱情药」的长袍，却不知那其实是致命的毒药。","src":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/sophocles/the-trachiniae/francis-storr","n":9876,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":778},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":3140},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1130},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1490},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":887},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":2451}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"medea","t":"Medea","z":"美狄亚","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"美狄亚为伊阿宋背叛了家乡。来到科林斯后，伊阿宋却要另娶公主，被抛弃的美狄亚展开了可怕的复仇。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":12925,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":964},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2845},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2023},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1747},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1324},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":2459},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":1563}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"bacchae","t":"The Bacchae","z":"酒神的伴侣","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"酒神狄俄尼索斯回到忒拜，国王彭透斯拒绝承认他是神。狂欢的女信徒们，和一场可怕的惩罚。（这部用的是巴克利 1850 年的译本）","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":11328,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":3007},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1153},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2822},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":938},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1426},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1982}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"trojan-women","t":"The Trojan Women","z":"特洛伊妇女","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"特洛伊城破，王后赫卡柏和城中的妇女们等着被分给希腊将领做奴隶。一部关于战争之后的反战悲剧。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":11479,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2167},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2161},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2494},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2289},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2368}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"alcestis","t":"Alcestis","z":"阿尔刻提斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"国王阿德墨托斯可以免于一死，前提是有人替他去死。只有妻子阿尔刻提斯愿意。后来，赫拉克勒斯来到了宫中。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":10310,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1841},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2006},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1153},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2650},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2660}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"hippolytus","t":"Hippolytus","z":"希波吕托斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"爱神阿佛洛狄忒要惩罚只敬奉处女神的希波吕托斯，让他的继母淮德拉疯狂地爱上了他。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":12119,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1073},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1711},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1695},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1640},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":3099},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1294},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":1607}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"electra-euripides","t":"Electra","z":"厄勒克特拉","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"同一个故事的欧里庇得斯版本：厄勒克特拉被迫嫁给一个穷农夫，住在乡下。弟弟回来后，姐弟俩的复仇显得更加残酷。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":11861,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1063},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2729},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2377},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1337},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2731},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1624}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"iphigenia-in-aulis","t":"Iphigenia in Aulis","z":"伊菲革涅亚在奥利斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"希腊大军因无风困在港口，先知说统帅阿伽门农必须献祭女儿。他以嫁给阿喀琉斯为借口，把女儿骗到了军营。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":14472,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1175},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":3309},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1822},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2817},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2156},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":3193}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"iphigenia-in-tauris","t":"Iphigenia in Tauris","z":"伊菲革涅亚在陶里斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"当年被女神救走的伊菲革涅亚，在遥远的蛮族之地当祭司，负责献祭外乡人。有一天，两个希腊青年被抓来了……","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":12527,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1102},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2019},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":3005},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2994},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1262},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":2145}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"ion","t":"Ion","z":"伊翁","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"在德尔斐神庙长大的孤儿伊翁，不知道自己的父母是谁。一位来求子的雅典王后，和他有着意想不到的关系。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":14879,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2035},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2004},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2192},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":3261},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2704},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":2683}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"helen","t":"Helen","z":"海伦","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"原来被带到特洛伊的只是海伦的幻影，真正的海伦一直在埃及。战争结束后，她的丈夫墨涅拉俄斯漂流到了埃及……","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":15333,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1579},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2183},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2148},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2227},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2095},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1794},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":1215},{"h":"Part 8","zh":"第8部分","n":2092}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"orestes","t":"Orestes","z":"俄瑞斯忒斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"杀母之后的俄瑞斯忒斯病倒在床，阿尔戈斯人要判他和姐姐死刑。走投无路的姐弟俩铤而走险。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":14925,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1257},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1402},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2680},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2117},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1187},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":2593},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":2238},{"h":"Part 8","zh":"第8部分","n":1451}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"hecuba","t":"Hecuba","z":"赫卡柏","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"特洛伊陷落后，老王后赫卡柏先失去了女儿，又发现托付给朋友的小儿子被杀，她决定亲手复仇。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":11306,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1907},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1897},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1592},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2440},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1749},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1721}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"andromache","t":"Andromache","z":"安德洛玛刻","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"赫克托耳的遗孀安德洛玛刻成了阿喀琉斯之子的女奴。主人的妻子嫉妒她，趁丈夫不在要置她母子于死地。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":11513,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1120},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1489},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1772},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":2696},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2055},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1382},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":999}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"heracles","t":"Heracles","z":"疯狂的赫拉克勒斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"赫拉克勒斯及时赶回家，从暴君手中救下了妻儿。可就在这时，女神赫拉让他陷入了疯狂。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":12762,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1042},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2259},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2544},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1837},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1261},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1912},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":1907}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"heracleidae","t":"The Heracleidae","z":"赫拉克勒斯的儿女","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"赫拉克勒斯死后，他的儿女被仇人一路追杀，逃到雅典求救。雅典要为保护他们而开战。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":9581,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":3387},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2244},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1290},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1235},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1425}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"suppliants-euripides","t":"The Suppliants","z":"乞援的妇女","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"七将攻忒拜失败后，阵亡将领的母亲们来到雅典，请求雅典国王忒修斯帮她们要回儿子的遗体。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":11051,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":3293},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":2278},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1637},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1454},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":1274},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":1115}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"phoenician-women","t":"The Phoenician Women","z":"腓尼基妇女","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"七将攻城前夕，母亲伊俄卡斯忒想让两个儿子和解，可兄弟俩谁也不肯让步。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":14714,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":1618},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1925},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1861},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1124},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2141},{"h":"Part 6","zh":"第6部分","n":2160},{"h":"Part 7","zh":"第7部分","n":1962},{"h":"Part 8","zh":"第8部分","n":1923}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"rhesus","t":"Rhesus","z":"瑞索斯","k":"Tragedy","zk":"悲剧","s":"特洛伊战争中的一个夜晚，色雷斯国王瑞索斯率军前来援助特洛伊，奥德修斯和狄俄墨得斯趁夜潜入敌营。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":8749,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":2021},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":991},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":1628},{"h":"Part 4","zh":"第4部分","n":1431},{"h":"Part 5","zh":"第5部分","n":2678}]},{"a":"euripides","id":"cyclops","t":"The Cyclops","z":"独眼巨人","k":"Satyr play","zk":"羊人剧（喜剧性）","s":"奥德修斯和船员被独眼巨人波吕斐摩斯抓住，他用酒把巨人灌醉，再刺瞎他的眼睛逃走。现存唯一完整的羊人剧。","src":"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/","n":6467,"parts":[{"h":"Part 1","zh":"第1部分","n":3249},{"h":"Part 2","zh":"第2部分","n":1139},{"h":"Part 3","zh":"第3部分","n":2079}]}]}